cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article below."
title: "NisslQuant: semi-automated quantification of dark-stained area in Nissl-stained histological sections"
abstract: "A Python tool that quantifies the dark-stained area fraction in Nissl-stained sections using dual-reference optical-density calibration, a reference-anchored midpoint threshold, multi-scale density decomposition and per-image uncertainty and quality control. The tool reports a threshold-position sensitivity range rather than claiming a unique optimum."
